{#
/**
 * @file
 * prose — the .content-page wrapper (docs/wysiwyg-output.md). The article
 * page layers give it their measure by parent (.news-article__flow > .content-page).
 */
#}
{# AN EMPTY BLOCK IS VISIBLE IN THE EDITOR (user call, 5 Nov 2026: "Make it
   so I can access zero height content blocks"): with no words — nothing,
   a stray <br>, a non-breaking space — the block wears .content-page--empty,
   and in the Canvas editor's frame base/prose.css gives it a height, a
   dashed line and a note, so it can be found, filled or deleted. On the
   page itself the class does nothing. #}
{% set words = text|render|replace({'&nbsp;': ' ', '\u00a0': ' '})|striptags|trim %}
<div class="content-page{% if words == '' %} content-page--empty{% endif %}" data-animate>
  {{ text }}
</div>
